    "created_at": "2016-02-05T06:27:47Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-02-05T06:27:47Z",
    "body": "We have:\n- **IDL attributes** are the script-exposed attributes/properties on interfaces like `HTMLInputElement` including non-elements `Document`.\n- A **content attribute** is an attribute in the DOM sense, i.e. something that an element has, as in `<html lang=\"en\">`.\n- \"Some IDL attributes are defined to **reflect** a particular content attribute. This means that on getting, the IDL attribute returns the current value of the content attribute, and on setting, the IDL attribute changes the value of the content attribute to the given value.\" ([source](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/infrastructure.html#reflect))\n\nFor `HTMLInputElement`, `value` is _not_ a reflected attribute, it has state independent of the content attribute. `defaultValue`, however, does reflect the `value` content attribute, if needed.\n\nHope that helps!\n\nSee also https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/551 for a similar kind of question.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
