    "created_at": "2016-02-07T14:07:35Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-02-07T14:07:35Z",
    "body": "It looks like that part of the test was added by @djc in https://github.com/w3c/web-platform-tests/commit/aeec0fc10b7f1f6a38e697e2ed6fd318a3f8acb0 in response to the https://github.com/whatwg/html/commit/193ac0acec7f9549a45470c90d8ba79f2faed7bc spec change.\n\nThis tests a behavior I didn't know about, sorry. If I had read the spec just a little beyond what you originally quoted, I would have seen that in the [default](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-input-value-default) and [default/on](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-input-value-default-on) states, the IDL attribute setter does indeed set the content attribute. And, for `type=checkbox` and `type=radio`, the state is default/on.\n",
